+# SIGAMON Underbuild Topology Design
+
+## Goal
+
+Make **Tools → Tambah Underbuild** resolve and follow the real JTM topology for Rencana Awal, Rencana Akhir, and Realisasi, including physical Existing poles and networks, without mutating the host JTM or mixing project locations.
+
+## Confirmed root cause
+
+`UnderbuildRangeDialog` still delegates graph construction to `DashboardNetworkRangeDialog`, whose source is selected through the single-value `DATA_LAYER_MAP`. The underbuild override temporarily rewrites that map once for the work layer and once for `JARINGAN_EKSISTING`, while filtering candidates through applied F11 state. The generic builder silently catches every per-feature exception and converts an empty result into the misleading implementation-level message `Layer JARINGAN_RENCANA belum memiliki segmen jaringan yang dapat diukur.`
+
+This creates four coupled failure modes:
+
+1. Rencana Awal and Rencana Akhir share one physical layer, but stage is resolved separately from the layer mapping.
+2. project and location filtering is implicit and has no per-candidate diagnostics;
+3. Existing is bolted on as a second graph instead of being a first-class source in one resolver;
+4. malformed or incompatible feature data disappears silently, making a visible network look absent.
+
+## Architecture
+
+Create `underbuild_topology.py` as a QGIS-free source of truth. It owns normalized `UnderbuildContext`, candidate scope decisions, stable node/edge identities, graph adjacency, shortest-path ambiguity counting, and idempotent partitioning of already-underbuilt versus new host edges. It never writes data.
+
+`plugin.py` adapts QGIS layers and features into resolver records. `UnderbuildRangeDialog` asks the resolver for the work layer plus Existing in a single operation, converts valid line geometry into topology records, builds one graph, and annotates nodes with matching stage/Existing poles and substations. It does not mutate `DATA_LAYER_MAP` and does not depend on which layer is selected or visible.
+
+The existing `ClickTransaction`, `_recalculate_underbuild_edit`, `delete_underbuild_path`, construction evaluator, BOQ adapter, and renderer remain the persistence path. Apply/delete validation is strengthened before the transaction, and structured Underbuild logging records context, candidate counts, selected path, transaction result, construction impact, and the root exception.
+
+## Scope and identity rules
+
+- Context is `project + location + stage`; village is never an identity boundary.
+- Rencana work features must match the selected Rencana Awal or Rencana Akhir. Legacy empty Rencana stage belongs only to Rencana Awal according to `stage_model.feature_stage`.
+- Realisasi work features must match Realisasi.
+- Existing is a physical reference, not a fourth stage. It must still match the selected project/location identity; stage is ignored only for Existing rows.
+- `id_proyek`/canonical project key and `id_lokasi` are authoritative. Location name is a legacy fallback only when the row has no location ID. A conflicting populated ID is rejected.
+- Endpoint UUID is authoritative. Display ID is fallback only when one side lacks UUID.
+- Host edge identity prefers feature UUID, then object UID/segment ID, then `(layer id, fid)`.
+
+## Graph and selection
+
+- Node coordinates are merged within the canvas-CRS tolerance, but edges from another scope never enter the candidate set.
+- Only JTM-capable edges are traversable. JTR-only edges cannot shortcut a route.
+- A unique shortest path is selected automatically. Multiple equal shortest paths remain an explicit user confirmation.
+- Point picking is deterministic: exact endpoint identity in context precedes distance; ambiguous co-located identities are shown to the user instead of selected randomly.
+- Preview is read-only and is cleared on Reset, Escape, Close, data-context change, or transaction completion.
+
+## Mutation and compatibility
+
+- Work-layer host JTM keeps its feature, geometry, UUID, endpoints, and distance; only Underbuild attributes are updated.
+- Existing JTM remains read-only and red solid. A stage-owned JTR overlay references the Existing host through `parent_uid`.
+- Reapplying the same host edge in the same stage/location is idempotent. Partial extension adds only uncovered edges.
+- One edge has one effective `Jarak (m)` source; overlays copy the host distance fields.
+- Existing underbuild data remains readable. No fields, tables, user settings, IDs, UUIDs, or project data are dropped or reset.
+- Apply and delete remain atomic through `ClickTransaction`; failure aborts all staged changes.
+
+## Construction and BOQ invariants
+
+- TR construction is derived from the underbuild graph, not nearest poles.
+- A through node is not forced to TR-3. Endpoints, bends, branches, and crossings continue through the SK-GM evaluator.
+- Two distinct underbuild runs terminating at one node may occupy two TR-3 slots.
+- Existing-pole TR stays on that physical Existing pole and is included once in BOQ.
+- Existing carrier alone never proves a JTM initial pull and cannot create TM-4X.
+- One physical TM-4X produces one BOQ occurrence.
+
+## Error and logging contract
+
+User messages identify stage and location and distinguish: no scoped JTM, invalid/malformed segments, disconnected endpoints, cross-scope endpoints, ambiguous routes, and already-underbuilt routes. Internal logs use the `SIGAMON Underbuild` channel and include action, project, location, stage, source layer, feature counts, rejection counts/reasons, selected edge identities, run UUID, transaction result, construction changes, BOQ impact, and root exception.
+
+## Verification
+
+Automated tests cover the 20 scenarios in the supplied specification, with QGIS-free behavior tests for resolver/graph/idempotency and source-contract tests for QGIS transaction, construction, renderer, cleanup, BOQ, and UI integration. Focused tests run first, followed by the entire unittest suite and syntax compilation. The release report records only commands actually run and their observed results.
